.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NQP11OPEN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqp11open ,
.Nm nqp11close ,
.Nm nqp11why ,
.Nm nqp11toks ,
.Nm nqp11login ,
.Nm nqp11keys ,
.Nm nqp11pub ,
.Nm nqp11sign ,
.Nm nqp11dec ,
.Nm nqp11gen
.Nd keys on a PKCS #11 token
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11open "const char *module" "nqp11 **p"
.Ft void
.Fn nqp11close "nqp11 *p"
.Ft unsigned long
.Fn nqp11why "const nqp11 *p"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11toks "nqp11 *p" "nqp11t *t" "size_t cap" "size_t *n"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11login "nqp11 *p" "unsigned long slot" "const char *pin" "size_t pinlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11keys "nqp11 *p" "nqp11k *k" "size_t cap" "size_t *n"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11pub "nqp11 *p" "const nqp11k *k" "uint8_t *pk" "size_t cap" "size_t *pklen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11sign "nqp11 *p" "const nqp11k *k" "const uint8_t *msg" "size_t n" "const uint8_t *ctx" "size_t ctxlen" "uint8_t *sig" "size_t cap" "size_t *siglen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11dec "nqp11 *p" "const nqp11k *k" "const uint8_t *ct" "size_t ctlen" "uint8_t *ss" "size_t sslen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqp11gen "nqp11 *p" "int kem" "int alg" "const char *label" "nqp11k *k"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions sign and decapsulate with private keys that stay on a
token: a smart card, a hardware security module, or a software token.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11open
loads the PKCS #11 module at the path
.Fa module
and starts it.
The path must have a folder in it; a bare name, which the system
would search for, is refused.
.Fn nqp11close
ends the session, if one is open, and unloads the module.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11toks
lists the tokens present, each an
.Vt nqp11t :
its slot, label, maker, model, serial number, and whether its keys
need the PIN.
.Fn nqp11login
opens a session with the token in
.Fa slot
and, when
.Fa pin
is not
.Dv NULL ,
logs the user in.
A handle has one session.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11keys
lists the private keys noqtis can use, each an
.Vt nqp11k :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct {
  int kem;           /* 1: alg is a nqkalg; 0: a nqsalg */
  int alg;
  unsigned long h;   /* the object, in this session */
  char label[65];
  uint8_t id[32];
  size_t idlen;
} nqp11k;
.Ed
.Pp
.Fn nqp11pub
gives the public key of one, in the form
.Xr nqvrfy 3
and
.Xr nqenc 3
take.
.Pp
.Fn nqp11sign
signs
.Fa msg
with a signature key (ML-DSA, SLH-DSA or Ed25519) and the context
.Fa ctx :
the signature is what
.Xr nqsign 3
makes, and
.Xr nqvrfy 3
checks it.
.Fn nqp11dec
decapsulates an ML-KEM ciphertext as
.Xr nqdec 3
does; the module must be of PKCS #11 version 3.2.
.Fn nqp11gen
makes a key pair on the token under
.Fa label ,
the private key marked never to leave it.
.Pp
A handle is for one thread at a time.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
on success.
.Dv NQEIO
when the module cannot be loaded or the token refuses;
.Fn nqp11why
then gives the module's own return value, a CKR number of the standard.
.Dv NQEDEC
for a library that is not a PKCS #11 module;
.Dv NQEVRFY
for a wrong or locked PIN;
.Dv NQENOSUP
when the token has not the mechanism, for an algorithm PKCS #11 has no
key type for, and on systems that load no shared libraries;
.Dv NQESTATE
before
.Fn nqp11login
or for a second one;
.Dv NQEBUF
with the count or the size needed in
.Fa *n ,
.Fa *pklen
or
.Fa *siglen ;
.Dv NQEARG
for a bad argument and a key of the wrong kind.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-token 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqdec 3 ,
.Xr nqsign 3
.Sh STANDARDS
OASIS PKCS #11 Specification Version 3.2.
